      "type": "descriptive",
      "question": "(a) If y1, y2 and y3 are uncorrelated observations with a common variance σ² and expectations E(y1) = β1 + β2, E(y2) = β1 + β3 and E(y3) = β1 + β2 then\n(i) show that l1 y1 + l2 y2 + l3 y3 is estimable if and only if l1 + l2 + l3 = 0\n(ii) find an unbiased estimate of β1\n(b) What do you understand by regression method of estimation? Apply regression method of estimation of population mean. Also obtain the expression of mean square error of the regression estimator and show that it is more efficient than the sample mean and ratio estimator under SRSWOR.",
